I think the definition of =93fi'i=94 on jbovlaste is just wrong.

The current definition is:
> vocative: hospitality - inhospitality; you are welcome/ make yourself
> at home.
This definition contradicts itself, since =93You=92re welcome!=94/=93You ar=
e
welcome!=94 is a response to =93Thank you=94, and is NOT used to indicate
hospitality. A simple =93Welcome!=94 is used for that instead. According to
the CLL <http://dag.github.io/cll/13/14/>, clearly the =93Welcome!=94
meaning is actually meant by =93fi'i=94 and not the =93You=92re welcome!=94
meaning.  But there are some Lojbanists that seem to confuse that. Part
of the confusion may be caused by this definition on jbovlaste.

I propose the following new definition:
> vocative: hospitality - inhospitality; =93Welcome! / Make yourself at
> home.

I propose to add the following notes for extra clarity:
> {fi'i} does not mean =93You=92re welcome=94. For =93You=92re welcome!=94 =
(as a
> response to =93Thank you!=94/{ki'e}), use {je'e} instead.
Probably a link to the relevant part of the CLL
<http://dag.github.io/cll/13/14/> could be added as well (if that
haven=92t already happened).

Normally, I make changes to jbovlaste directly, but I make an exception
for cmavo and gismu, because messing with their definitions is serious
business. I want to hear your opinions first.

